<title>NAMIBIA: FIRST NAMIBIAN CENTRAL BANK GOVERNOR APPOINTED.</title>
<headline>FIRST NAMIBIAN CENTRAL BANK GOVERNOR APPOINTED.</headline>
<dateline>WINDHOEK 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Namibia on Thursday appointed its first Namibian governor, effective from January 1.</p>
<p>Current central bank deputy governor Tom Alweendo will fill the post, replacing Malaysian Jaafar Ahmed.</p>
<p>Alweendo has held the post of deputy governor since 1993.</p>
<p>Until Alweendo takes his post, the position will be filled by manager of money and banking, Lazarus Ipangelwa.</p>
